---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Arcbuildr"
  description="What Arcbuildr collects when you use this site, why, who else sees it, and how to ask us to delete it."
  noindex
>
  <article class="wrap privacy">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: October 25, 2026</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="p-who">
      <h2 id="p-who">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Arcbuildr is a personal brand service run by Zyade and Hanane. To reach us about your
        details, email [email] or send a DM to @arcbuildr on Instagram.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="p-collect">
      <h2 id="p-collect">What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        What you type in the form: your name, email, Instagram handle, business and, if you fill it
        in, what you want your personal brand to do for your business. We also save which link you
        came from (such as our Instagram bio), the page you came from, and the time you sent the
        form.
      </p>
      <p>
        The booking tool records the time you pick. Our site statistics count visits to each page
        and do not use cookies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="p-why">
      <h2 id="p-why">Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>
        To prepare for the call and hold it, and to see how many people visit the site and book. We
        don't use your details for anything else.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="p-others">
      <h2 id="p-others">Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>These services handle your details for us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Cloudflare hosts this site and counts visits without cookies.</li>
        <li>Notion stores what you type in the form.</li>
        <li>Resend sends us an email when a new form comes in.</li>
        <li>Cal.com runs the booking calendar on the next page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don't sell your details or share them with anyone else.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="p-keep">
      <h2 id="p-keep">How long we keep it, and how to ask us to delete it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your details while we talk about working together and while we work with you. To
        have them deleted, email [email] or send us a DM, and we delete them from Notion and from
        our email.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    padding-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-2xl);
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: var(--rule-thin);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }
  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }
</style>
